Authors of [PS22] investigate developers’ interaction with code recommendation systems and their impact on flow
by modeling user behavior while using tools such as Copilot. Findings show that developers spend an average of 51.5%
of their coding session time in LLM interaction states, such as verifying suggestions, prompt crafting, and deferring
